<div class="page-header">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>About Bizbox</h1>
</div>

<div style="max-width: 720px;">
    <p>Starting a small business usually means sourcing equipment from several different vendors, comparing quality across sources with no single reference point, and figuring out what's actually needed before you can open. That friction alone discourages a lot of people from starting.</p>

    <p>Bizbox addresses this by giving each business type a curated, ready-to-buy equipment list. Choose a business type, review what's needed, and check out &mdash; either piece by piece or as a complete starter kit.</p>

    <h3>What Bizbox supports</h3>
    <p>Bizbox currently covers four business types: Coffee Shop, Bakery, Restaurant, and Salon. Each comes with its own curated catalog of the equipment typically required to open that kind of business.</p>

    <h3>Beyond the initial purchase</h3>
    <p>Bizbox also includes a resale marketplace, where users can list equipment they no longer need, and an upgrade-notification system that alerts owners when a newer model of something they've purchased becomes available.</p>

    <h3>Scope</h3>
    <p>This is an academic e-commerce project built with ASP.NET Core MVC. Domestic payments are processed through eSewa and Khalti sandbox integrations; other elements &mdash; including manufacturer listings and international payment &mdash; are simulated for the purposes of this project's scope.</p>
</div>
